<title>LATVIA: CENTRAL BANK FOREIGN ASSETS FALL IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>CENTRAL BANK FOREIGN ASSETS FALL IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Latvian central bank said on Monday that its foreign assets fell in june by 1.2 million lats to 532.602 million lats.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that its foreign liabilities also fell, by 3.3 million lats to 134.956 million lats. It said that both falls came as the bank continued to pay back International Monetary Fund (IMF) credits.  </p>
<p>The amount of lats in circulation came to 310.04 million lats, a rise of 13.7 million lats or 4.6 percent due to a seasonal rise in demand.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
